<title>INDIA: India RBI raises 29.36 bln rupees in 14-day bills.</title>
<headline>India RBI raises 29.36 bln rupees in 14-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it  accepted competitive bids for 29.36 billion rupees at an auction of  14-day treasury bills on Friday.</p>
<p>The RBI also accepted one non-competitive bid for 750 million rupees.  The total face value of bills issued was 31.09 billion.</p>
<p>The weighted average cut-off rate was 99.81 rupees.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22=2654 9000</p>
